-- ============================================================================
-- Organizations from Adaptive Rec Hub
-- ============================================================================
-- The owner, 2026-11-03: add every program listed on adaptiverechub.org/programs
-- that the club does not have, with the location its page shows, read in the
-- owner's browser on 2026-11-02 (612 of 615 pages; 3 would not open). This is
-- the owner's choice to take a directory's word for these, where the club's
-- own organizations come from their own sites. Fixed: hhttps and tracking in
-- links, plain misspellings of names, cities and streets. Left out, for the
-- owner: anything outside the US, without a city and a state, or whose state
-- or ZIP disagree. Chapters of one organization are one, with a place each.
--
-- Only those whose own site, read 2026-11-03, speaks of spinal cord injury or
-- disease (56) or of wheelchair users or physical disabilities (147), as the
-- owner asked. The rest wait for the owner; parks go on the map, not here.
--
-- A street is a place's address only when it is one: a mailbox, or a name with
-- no number, puts the pin at the city's middle. The Geocode workflow looks the
-- addresses up (500 a day), so pins become exact over a day or two.
-- Never doubles: an organization already here by name or alias is skipped,
-- including any added in the app since.
-- ============================================================================

